# handle-drag-out (h7-plane): the diamond dragged 12 px past the canvas's
# right edge (1423) out to x=1435 and held: the handle keeps following
# (the pan's pointer capture retargets the canvas moves; h=11.14), the
# camera unchanged, grab-active with the h,k rulers out. The target stays
# inside the 1440 viewport: past it SDL's web moves stop reaching the port
# (probed: web h=10.40 vs native/ref h=11.44 at x=1500, all engines — a
# stack-level web-only edge difference, recorded in h7-plane.md), while
# the capture path itself is what this state proves. Ends held; the
# release past the edge still ends the drag (probed: modes cleared,
# cursor pan), but its hover state is lag-divergent by construction, so no
# release read belongs to this state.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
query func=x2&a=2&h=1&k=-3
wait 500
move 978 640
wait 200
down
wait 150
move 1435 640 over 160
wait 300
shot handle-drag-out
up
